0.02420866,0.01991474,0.05676512,-0.12919018,0.03649519,-0.05601428,0.1880769,0.02918993,-0.04128134,-0.02976117,-0.00957345,0.02269972,0.07010087,0.02399854,-0.0198788,0.04549122,0.04587777,0.00101303,0.04128401,0.03196301,-0.01390024,0.0347881,-0.03631109,0.00349241,-0.00573417,0.01884728,-0.05024951,0.00071766,0.13004273,-0.04585788,-0.02914987,-0.02295105,0.03304147,-0.01044778,0.02654122,-0.03133902,-0.01368185,0.03894488,-0.00779007,-0.01779506,-0.02606986,-0.03329482,0.03469672,-0.00920297,0.0145702,-0.0150122,0.10868673,0.02982428,-0.00502645],"last_embed":{"tokens":468,"hash":"1agl9r6"}}},"text":null,"length":0,"last_read":{"hash":"1agl9r6","at":1780752824347},"key":"docs/PSModulesHelp/PSReminderLite/README.md#PSReminderLite","lines":[1,547],"size":22253,"outlinks":[{"title":"![PSGallery Downloads","target":"https://img.shields.io/powershellgallery/dt/PSReminderLite.png?style=for-the-badge&label=Downloads","line":3},{"title":"![PSGallery Version","target":"https://img.shields.io/powershellgallery/v/PSReminderLite.png?style=for-the-badge&label=PowerShell%20Gallery","line":3},{"title":"Reminder Icon","target":"images/icons8-reminder-85.png","line":39,"embedded":true},{"title":"Add-PSReminder","target":"docs/Add-PSReminder.md","line":43},{"title":"Export-PSReminderDatabase","target":"docs/Export-PSReminderDatabase.md","line":44},{"title":"Export-PSReminderPreference","target":"docs/Export-PSReminderPreference.md","line":45},{"title":"Get-AboutPSReminder","target":"docs/Get-AboutPSReminder.md","line":46},{"title":"Get-PSReminder","target":"docs/Get-PSReminder.md","line":47},{"title":"Get-PSReminderDBInformation","target":"docs/Get-PSReminderDBInformation.md","line":48},{"title":"Get-PSReminderPreference","target":"docs/Get-PSReminderPreference.md","line":49},{"title":"Get-PSReminderTag","target":"docs/Get-PSReminderTag.md","line":50},{"title":"Import-FromTickleDatabase","target":"docs/Import-FromTickleDatabase.md","line":51},{"title":"Import-PSReminderDatabase","target":"docs/Import-PSReminderDatabase.md","line":52},{"title":"Initialize-PSReminderDatabase","target":"docs/Initialize-PSReminderDatabase.md","line":53},{"title":"Move-PSReminder","target":"docs/Move-PSReminder.md","line":54},{"title":"Remove-PSReminder","target":"docs/Remove-PSReminder.md","line":55},{"title":"Set-PSReminder","target":"docs/Set-PSReminder.md","line":56},{"title":"38;5;192m\"\r\n    'Personal' = \"`e[96m\"\r\n    'Priority' = \"`e[1;3;38;5;199m\"\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\nYou can use native ANSI sequences or `$PSStyle` references. You can add as many tags as you would like.\r\n\r\n```powershell\r\n$PSReminderTag.Add(\"Event\",$PSStyle.Foreground.Yellow)\r\n```\r\n\r\nRun `Get-PSReminderTag` to see the current tags.\r\n\r\n![Get-PSReminderTag","target":"images/psremindertags.png","line":110},{"title":"Display reminders","target":"images/get-psreminder-by-tag.png","line":128,"embedded":true},{"title":"0m\")\r\n            }\r\n        }\r\n        return $r\r\n    }\r\n} #close PSReminderPreference class\r\n\r\nUpdate-TypeData -TypeName PSReminder -DefaultDisplayPropertySet ID, Date, Event, Comment -Force\r\nUpdate-TypeData -TypeName PSReminder -MemberType AliasProperty -MemberName Name -Value Event -Force\r\nUpdate-TypeData -Typename PSReminder -MemberType ScriptProperty -MemberName Countdown -value {\r\n    $ts = $this.Date - (Get-Date)\r\n    if ($ts.TotalMinutes -lt 0) {\r\n        $ts = New-TimeSpan -Minutes 0\r\n    }\r\n    $ts\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\nBy default, expired reminders are not displayed unless explicitly requested.\r\n\r\n```powershell\r\nGet-PSReminder -Expired\r\n```\r\n\r\nThese items remain in the primary event table. It is recommended that you periodically archive expired reminders. You can do this with the `Move-PSReminder` command. This command has an alias of 'Archive-PSReminder`.\r\n\r\n```powershell\r\nGet-PSReminder -Expired | Move-PSReminder\r\n```\r\n\r\nThis is a manual process because you may want to review and adjust expired events before archiving them. If you want to automate the process, add the above command to your PowerShell profile script.\r\n\r\n> *There is no module command to move an archived reminder back to the event table.*\r\n\r\nYou can use `Get-PSReminder` to view archived events.\r\n\r\n```shell\r\nPS C:\\> Get-PSReminder -Archived | Select-Object -last 3\r\n\r\nID   Event              Comment Date                 ArchivedDate\r\n--   -----              ------- ----                 ------------\r\n1084 PSTweetChat                5/3/2024 1:00:00 PM  7/22/2024 2:05:01 PM\r\n1101 Onramp 25 Planning         5/31/2024 2:00:00 PM 7/22/2024 2:05:01 PM\r\n1085 PSTweetChat                6/7/2024 1:00:00 PM  7/23/2024 8:15:22 AM\r\n```\r\n\r\n## :tada: Display Formatting\r\n\r\nThe default display using `Get-PSReminder` uses a custom formatting file. The default view will show expired items using a default ANSI escape sequence.\r\n\r\n![Expired formatting","target":"images/expired-psreminder.png","line":269},{"title":"PSReminder display","target":"images/psreminder-formatting.png","line":323,"embedded":true},{"title":"Get-PSReminderPreference","target":"images/get-psreminderpreference.png","line":362,"embedded":true},{"title":"custom verbose messaging","target":"images/verbose.png","line":524,"embedded":true},{"title":"Icons8","target":"https://icons8.com","line":543},{"title":"Module icon","target":"https://icons8.com/icon/mYoNj7pHoJ-q/reminder","line":543},{"title":"Reminder Icon","target":"images/icons8-reminder-85.png","line":543,"embedded":true}],"class_name":"SmartBlock"},
